-- title:
--   Serre–Tate lifting along one small surjection
-- statement:
--   Let $q$ be a prime, let $B$ be an Artinian local commutative ring with algebraically closed residue field, and let $B_1$ be a commutative $B$-algebra such that the structure map $B \to B_1$ is surjective, its kernel $J$ is nilpotent and satisfies the smallness condition $J \cdot \mathfrak m_B = 0$, and such that the image of $q$ in $B$ is nilpotent. Let $f_1 : A_1 \to \operatorname{Spec} B_1$ be a morphism of schemes carrying a commutative relative group law $L_1$ (a functorial group structure on the sets of sections $\{\varphi : T \to A_1 \mid \varphi \text{ followed by } f_1 = t\}$, natural in the $\operatorname{Spec} B_1$-scheme $t : T \to \operatorname{Spec} B_1$), and assume $f_1$ is smooth and proper with connected fibres and admits a relative group law. Let $F$ be a commutative $2$-dimensional formal group law over $B$, and let $\theta_1$ be a system of formal coordinates for $f_1$ in $2$ variables, i.e. an assignment, to each $B_1$-algebra $B'$ and each pair of elements of $B'$, of a point of $A_1$ over $\operatorname{Spec} B'$, which is compatible with $B_1$-algebra maps on nilpotent tuples and which, for every ideal $J' \subseteq B'$ with $J'^{\,n+1} = 0$, restricts to a bijection from tuples in $J'$ onto the $J'$-infinitesimal points, transporting the $n$-truncated addition of $F \otimes_B B_1$ to $L_1$. Assume further that every point $P$ of $A_1$ over the spectrum of a $B_1$-algebra $C$ killed by some power $q^m$ in $L_1$ is infinitesimal along some nilpotent ideal of $C$, and that $F$ has height $4$ over every residue field: for each field $k$ and each surjective ring homomorphism $\rho : B \to k$, the quotient of $k[[X_1, X_2]]$ by the ideal generated by the components of the $q$-fold iterate $[q]_{F \otimes_\rho k}$ has $k$-dimension $q^4$. Then there exist a bare deformation $D$ of $(f_1, L_1)$ over $B$ — a smooth proper morphism $D.f : D.A \to \operatorname{Spec} B$ with connected fibres, carrying a commutative relative group law $D.L$, together with a morphism $g : A_1 \to D.A$ making the square over $\operatorname{Spec} B_1 \to \operatorname{Spec} B$ cartesian and compatible with the two group laws — and formal coordinates $\theta$ for $D.f$ in $2$ variables which present $D.L$ by the formal group law $F$ in the above sense and which lift $\theta_1$, in the sense that for every ring that is an algebra over $B$ and over $B_1$ compatibly and every pair of nilpotent elements $s$, the point $\theta_1(s)$ followed by $g$ equals $\theta(s)$.
--
--   This is the one-step essential surjectivity in the Serre–Tate theory of local moduli: along a single small surjection of Artinian local rings, an abelian scheme with prescribed formal group law lifts together with its formal coordinates. It is the inductive step used by [`GoodReductionJacobian.BareDeformation.exists_isFormalCoordinates_liftsCoordinates_of_isArtinianRing_of_isAlgClosed`](thm.html#GoodReductionJacobian.BareDeformation.exists_isFormalCoordinates_liftsCoordinates_of_isArtinianRing_of_isAlgClosed), which iterates it over a chain of small surjections.
